                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bastion is my first Supergiant Games game that I have ever played, and I had a wonderful time playing this game until the very end. You start with a silent protagonist with an old man called Rucks narrating what you should do. He narrates in combat, reacts to your weapon of choice and ability customizations, and narrates the story to you. The story is absolutely wonderful, and I was hooked at its mysterious element since the beginning. I will certainly return to this game, as the story has multiple endings, allowing me to have a fresh experience in the New Game Plus mode. \n\nMoving on to combat, it does offer a ton of variety of playstyles and ways to finish each section smoothly. Weapon upgrades don't cost that much, and each upgrade is a banger and can make your run easier and more fun to play with. I am amused with the enemy variety, as there are various ways to defeat them, and it requires a few tactical moves to counter attacks, block them, and strike them at the perfect time. \n\nThe art style is beautiful for a first game from Supergiant Games. I really love its details too, as it's also part of the storytelling. The music is vibrant and aligns its tone to the story, which adds an emotional influence to the player. \n\nThe New Game Plus features have exactly what you need, so I'll definitely play this again one day. \n\nOne of the problems that I had with this game is that the narration happens as well during combat when my focus is towards survival because it happens sometimes when there are too many enemies, in which I will miss a bit of context to the story. For me, I think the keyboard controls are weird in a sense, but they work regardless. I think using a controller is the best option to play the game, but a keyboard and mouse are fine as well. \n\nOverall, I finally understand why it has overwhelmingly positive reviews, and I have played and witnessed the beauty of this game. 9/10 and will play it again. This game is surprisingly well made considering it's the first game by Supergiant Games and came out in 2011.\n\nhttps://x.com/ShiroSaints777/status/2110798204048728199?s=20",
